{
  "case_id": "2004-04-480",
  "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer Studios, Inc. (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Copyright infringement is the only commercially significant use of the Grokster and StreamCast services, and that is no accident. Respondents deliberately set out to capture a clientele of known infringers to stock their services with infringing content, they intentionally and directly promote the infringing use of the service, they support infringing use of the service, and they directly"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I just interrupt for the one -- you said \"the only significant use.\" There's a footnote in the red brief that says the figure is some 2.6 billion legitimate uses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: We'll hear argument now in number 04-480, MGM Studios versus Grokster, Limited."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But there could be. There could be, both with respect to material in the public domain and with respect to people who authorize the transmission."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: It's not clear -- it's not clear to me from your brief, focusing on the contributory aspect of it, not -- and not the inducement part of it -- it's not clear to me from your brief what your test is."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The decision below allows companies, like Respondents, to build a business model out of copyright infringement without fear of secondary liability."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It came from a study by Petitioners' experts of the actual operation of the system."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Ninth Circuit got it wrong because it thought that test was satisfied by a combination of two things: being able to point out that there were such things as public-domain works or authorized sharing of the Wilco album, for example, and anecdotal evidence that you could actually do that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there ought to be enough room for -- under the Sony test, before you reach actual inducement, to capture somebody where they've clearly set out, as a business model, to deal with the infringing uses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Taranto",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because Respondent's software products are tools of autonomous communications that have large and growing legitimate uses, their distribution is protected under the clear Sony rule."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes, but active inducement is a doctrine that's been employed to curb the intentional encouragement of noninfringing uses, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That, Mr. Taranto, is something I find very puzzling."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What is -- what is the answer to Justice Kennedy's question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: -- but what you have -- what you want to do is to say that unlawfully expropriated property can be used by the owner of the instrumentality as part of the startup capital for his product."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Then perhaps there should be a trial so it would all come out."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Why isn't this a classic willful-ignorance case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. TARANTO: I think that they can certainly argue, with an affirmance by this Court, that all of the past acts, to use the District Court's term, constitute a basis for a -- inducement liability."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0003-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Sony said that the staple article-of-commerce doctrine, not copyright law, generally, and not secondary liability, generally, but the staple article-of-commerce doctrine, the noninducement part of the analysis, has got to strike an effective balance -- a real balance that provides effective protection of copyright, as well as protecting unrelated lines of commerce."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, their rule is a rule of immunity. It's a free pass. It says, all you've got to do is speculate about noninfringing use, and you can continue with infringement, ad infinitum. And that's not a rule that protects innovation; that's a rule that destroys innovation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "technological innovation moving towards legitimate means of distributing this -- of distributing, in a digital format, music and movies through the kinds of companies that filed amicus briefs and that are trying to do this legitimately."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0003-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the recording industry has lost 25 percent of its revenue since the onslaught of these services."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-04-480",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "164d0d530150985c1aa985455118207fdf0c91270fe1a5f8e873e947e5631ca4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-164d0d530150-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:14 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    }
  ],
